{"name":"Ripple","hex":"#d3dcdc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ripple","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village and civil parish in Dover district, Kent, England .","A village and civil parish in Malvern Hills district, Worcestershire, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ripple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Capillary wave","blocks":[{"text":"A capillary wave is a wave traveling along the phase boundary of a fluid, whose dynamics and phase velocity are dominated by the effects of surface tension."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/2006-01-14_Surface_waves.jpg/330px-2006-01-14_Surface_waves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capillary_wave"},{"title":"Gravitational wave","blocks":[{"text":"Gravitational waves are waves of spacetime curvature produced by the relative motion of gravitating masses and which propagate away at the speed of light. They were first predicted by Albert Einstein as a consequence of his general theory of relativity, appearing as \"ripples in spacetime curvature\".\nHundreds of these gravitational waves have since then been observed, first indirectly using binary-pulsar observations and, since 2015, directly through dedicated observatories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Warped_Space_and_Time_Around_Colliding_Black_Holes_%28Courtesy_Caltech-MIT-LIGO_Laboratory%2C_produced_by_SXS_project%29.webm/330px--Warped_Space_and_Time_Around_Colliding_Black_Holes_%28Courtesy_Caltech-MIT-LIGO_Laboratory%2C_produced_by_SXS_project%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravitational_wave"},{"title":"Ripple (electrical)","blocks":[{"text":"Ripple in electronics is the residual periodic variation of the DC voltage within a power supply which has been derived from an alternating current (AC) source. This ripple is due to incomplete suppression of the alternating waveform after rectification. Ripple voltage originates as the output of a rectifier or from generation and commutation of DC power."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ripple_(electrical)"},{"title":"Ripple (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Ripple is an American television drama series created by Michele Giannusa. The eight-episode season premiered on Netflix on December 3, 2025, starring Ian Harding, Julia Chan, Sydney Agudong, Frankie Faison, Vanessa Smythe, and Robert Bazzochi."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ripple_(TV_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Ripples_Lifjord.jpg/500px-Ripples_Lifjord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Ripples_Lifjord.jpg/1280px-Ripples_Lifjord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Ripples_Lifjord.jpg/500px-Ripples_Lifjord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ripples on Lifjord in Øksnes Municipality, Norway","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARipples_Lifjord.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Multy_droplets_impact.JPG/500px-Multy_droplets_impact.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Multy_droplets_impact.JPG/1280px-Multy_droplets_impact.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Multy_droplets_impact.JPG/500px-Multy_droplets_impact.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Capillary waves produced by droplet impacts on the interface between water and air.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMulty_droplets_impact.J